{"name":"Cry Me a River","hex":"#427898","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cry me a river","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To weep profusely or excessively in the presence of another person.","To try to obtain the sympathy of another person by complaining or sniveling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry_me_a_river"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cry Me a River (Arthur Hamilton song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cry Me a River\" is an American popular song, written by Arthur Hamilton, first published in 1953 and made famous in 1955 with the version by Julie London."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Arthur_Hamilton_song)","wikidata":"Q2530778"},{"title":"Cry Me a River (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cry Me a River is an album led by pianist John Hicks, with bassist Dwayne Burno and drummer Victor Lewis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(album)","wikidata":"Q39070856"},{"title":"Cry Me a River (Justin Timberlake song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cry Me a River\" is a song by American singer Justin Timberlake for his debut solo album, Justified (2002). It was thought to be inspired by Timberlake's former relationship with singer Britney Spears. Jive Records released the song to contemporary hit and rhythmic radio in the United States on November 25, 2002, as the album's second single. Accompanied by an electric piano, beatbox, guitars, synthesizers, Arabian-inspired riffs and Gregorian chants, \"Cry Me a River\" is a funk, pop and R&B song about a brokenhearted man who moves on from his past."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)","wikidata":"Q572144"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg/250px-Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg/250px-Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c4/JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg/250px-JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c4/JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg/250px-JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/73/Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png/250px-Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/73/Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png/250px-Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACry_Me_a_River_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu